&+Wfight against orc barbarians so she could see Pelor, but she triumphed
&+Winstead. Victorious, she founded several Ecaterine convents.
   &+WWhen she was thirty-seven, Ecaterine decided to establish one of her
&+Wconvents near Barovia. Despite being nightly accosted by vicious wolves,
&+Whaunts, and the occasional undead avenger, Ecaterine managed to accomplish
&+Wher goal. After making certain that the convent, located in a well-defended
&+Wtower, was secure against the kind of threats she had come to expect, she
&+Wleft to report her success. When she returned a month later, she found the
&+Wtower a burnt out shell with nothing inhabiting it but the ghosts of slain
&+Wsisters. Ecaterine is said to have gone mad, and none ever saw her alive
&+Wagain, though it was whispered she was captured and buried alive in a prison
&+Wbelow Castle Ravenloft. All that remains is this shroud.
