E
memory barov ravenovia~
&+CA ghostly scene from Strahd Von Zarovich's perspective, many years ago,
&+Ctransforms the immediate area into the grand foyer of Castle Ravenloft.

&+LThe year is 320 BC and a young prince Strahd, still in his teens, shuffles
&+Lthrough the gates bearing the weight of his mortally wounded father, King
&+LBarov. Drenched in blood, Strahd slows the king's slump to the ground and
&+Lviciously tears free his father's breastplate before looking on in shock,
&+Ltears starting to swell. Queen Ravenovia forces her way past her queens-
&+Lguard and crumbles beside them, clutching the weakened king in his final
&+Lmoment...

&+C'My sweet king.. don't go..' weeps a distraught Ravenovia.

&+CKing Barov coughs and turns, looking up at you. He mutters 'Strahd, my son..
&+Chave the Tergs been stopped?'

&+CRestraining a growing rage, you muster the words 'Yes, father.'

&+CKing Barov's face relaxes into a sedated smile for a moment.
&+C'Strahd..' &Nhe calls.
&+C'Yes, father?' &Nyou reply, but he does not respond.
&+C'Father?' you repeat with more intensity.
A teardrop falls from your cheek, landing on the king's face without a flinch.

&+CQueen Ravenovia sits up abruptly, her face stained with her husband's blood.
&+C'Barov?' she asks abruptly.
&+C'BAROV!' she repeats, before descending into hysterics.
~
