E
memory sergei~
&+CA ghostly scene from Strahd Von Zarovich's perspective many years ago
&+Ctransforms the immediate area into the ballroom of Castle Ravenloft, where
&+Cthe Count and his brother Sergei are hosting a celebration of recent conquest.
&+CA beautiful maiden stands out - a common girl dressed in red, dancing alone.

&+L'May I have this dance?' you ask, with a tap on the strange girl's shoulder.
&+LShe gasps with her hand on her chest and says 'My king, of course!'
&+LYou feign a comforting chuckle and take her hand. The crowded dancefloor
&+Lquickly opens and, for the next several minutes, you and Tatyana share the
&+Lgaze of every reveller at the party. She praises your conquests and laments
&+Lthe loss of her father (a soldier recruited to your army years ago), then
&+Lpolitely accepts your invitation to dinner. Arms linked, you walk together
&+Lto the banquet hall.

&+LAs you gentlemanly hold open one of the double-doors, the other suddenly
&+Lswings back, briefly startling Tatyana. Her arm loosens from yours as she
&+Lsees your grinning brother, Sergei; eyes locked with hers and sparkling with
&+La charming mischief.

&+CThe scene suddenly bursts into mist before quickly reshaping into the crowded
&+Cchapel of Castle Ravenloft. Bathed in the prismatic sunshine of the colorful
&+Cstained glass windows, a white-dressed Tatyana and her beloved Sergei stand
&+Cface-to-face, holding hands before a smiling priest.

&+L'You may now kiss the bride.' &+Lsays the priest with a gentle nod.
&+LAs Tatyana slowly lifts her veil to kiss her groom, she's met with a look of
&+Lshock and pain. Blood spurts from Sergei's stomach onto Tatyana's dress as
&+Lyou yank your blade from his back. She turns, horrified, and runs.

&+LYou chase her through the chaos of the screaming crowd, begging her to listen.
&+L'Let me explain!' you roar.
&+L'You belong with me! Not that boy, Sergei!'
&+LTatyana doesn't listen. She races through the banquet hall and onto the
&+Lbalcony, where she watched so many sunsets with Sergei. Cornered, she turns
&+Ltowards you and grasps the edge.
&+L'Let me show you that you should be mine..' you say, ignoring the arrows being
&+Lfired into your back by your own guards.
&+L'I will never be yours, Strahd Von Zarovich' she says boldly, before closing
&+Lher eyes and falling backwards into the darkness.
~
