mystical scroll favor high guard~
                                             ___________________________
   _______________________-------------------                           `\
 /:--__                                                                  |
||< > |                                   _______________________________/
| \__/_________________-------------------                             |
|                                                                      |
 |  To the One Whose Courage Whispers Louder Than Fear,                |
  |                                                                     |
 |  It is with deliberate purpose and the Count's discerning eye       |
 |  that I extend to you a solemn invitation - to stand among          |
 |  the ranks of the Royal Guard of Castle Ravenloft, the vigilant     |
 |  few who serve under the shadow and glory of Count Strahd von       |
 |  Zarovich, Lord of Barovia and Master of this realm.                |
 |                                                                     |
 |  You forgive, I trust, the formal tone of this summons; such is     |
 |  the way of our House. Those who guard the immortal Count do not    |
 |  merely bear arms - they bear honor, silence, and eternity. Within |
|  the storm-wreathed towers of Ravenloft, a thousand candles burn    |
|  in remembrance of those who served before you. Their names echo    |
|  through the stones - though few now live to speak them.            |
|                                                                     |
|  Should you accept, you will find your training most rigorous.      |
|  You will learn the stillness of the grave and the swiftness        |
|  of the wolf. You will stand your watch beneath windows that gaze    |
|  upon endless mists, and your heart will learn to beat not in fear,  |
|  but in reverence. The Lord of Barovia rewards loyalty beyond mortal |
|  measure; even death bends knee to his favor.                        |
|                                                                     |
|  Know, however, that service here is not for the faint or fickle.   |
|  Many have walked through the gates of Ravenloft with trembling     |
 |  hands and bright ambition - only to find the weight of the Count's |
 |  gaze too vast to bear. Yet those who endure, who learn to love the |
 |  hush of the crypt and the thunder of his approach, find themselves |
 |  remade. You will no longer belong to the fleeting world beyond     |
 |  these mountains. You will belong to him - and in that belonging,   |
 |  find purpose everlasting.                                          |
 |                                                                     |
 |  Present yourself to the High Chancellor upon the next moonless     |
 |  night. Inquire, then, about the fortunes of Ravenloft and I shall  |
 |  personally present your trials. Return, finally, with five earned  |
 |  fortunes along with this note, and I will see that your armor      |
 |  gleams crimson in His honor.                                       |
 |                                                                    |
 |         &+L,_  &+g`{&+r@&+g)'                       &+b/R /4 /-/ /4 /> / /\/&N     |
 |        &+L<)')-&+g//`                       &+BHigh Chamberlain Rahadin&N     |
 |        &+L(_.\\=&N                                                     |
 |          &+L"&+g//&+L`&N                              _______________________|_
 |  ___________________-----------------------                         `\
 |/`--_                                                                  |
 ||[ ]||                                          ______________________/
