                                             ___________________________
   _______________________-------------------                           `\
 /:--__                                                                  |
||< > |                                   _______________________________/
| \__/_________________-------------------                             |
|                                                                      |
|   To the Silent Hand Who Moves Unseen,                               |
 |                                                                    |
 |  Your name has reached my ear, whispered in the hush between       |
 |  dying breaths. It comes to me on the wind that howls through      |
 |  the Alduran Mountains - soft, but persistent. Such whispers       |
 |  are seldom false. Thus, I address you with an offer few would     |
  |  dare to make, and fewer still would survive to refuse.            |
  |                                                                    |
  |  Within the veiled courts of Barovia, beneath the Count's eternal  |
  |  gaze, there exists a concordance of those who serve not with      |
  |  oaths or banners, but with silence and precision. We are known    |
 |  to none, save our own, and even among us names are seldom spoken.  |
 |  The Count calls us his Whispered Blades. Others, in their fear     |
 |  and ignorance, speak of a guild of assassins. We prefer "artists." |
 |                                                                    |
 |  To join us is to shed the budens of conscience and hesitation.    |
 |  We deal in the currency of inevitability. Each task is not an     |
 |  act of murder, but a correction of imbalance - the removal of     |
 |  a piece no longer fit upon the board. In Barovia, mercy is myth;  |
 |  necessity is law. You, it seems, understand this already.         |
 |                                                                    |
  |  Membership brings privilege. You will walk unseen through the     |
  |  Castle's corridors, dine in silence with nobility who never       |
  |  sense your shadow. Wealth, protection, and purpose will be        |
  |  yours - but they come bound in blood. Once your blade drinks      |
  |  in service to the Count, it may never again be drawn without      |
  |  His will. Betrayal is not punished; it is erased.                |
 |                                                                    |
 |  Should you accept, travel alone to gallery where the cellar       |
 |  meets the stairs, to seek my private audience. There, under       |
 |  mask of shadow, you will ask me of the fortunes of Ravenloft      |
 |  and receive your first five marks. Return to me this scroll      |
 |  and five fortunes of Ravenloft and then we shall see whether     |
  |  your silence cuts as sharply as your steel.                      |
 |                                                                   |
 |         &+L,_  &+g`{&+r@&+g)'                       &+b/R /4 /-/ /4 /> / /\/&+L    &N |
 |        &+L<)')-&+g//`                       &+BHigh Chamberlain Rahadin&+L    &N |
 |        &+L(_.\\=                                                  &N   |
 |          &+L"&+g//&+L` &N                             _______________________|_
 |  ___________________-----------------------                         `\
 |/`--_                                                                  |
 ||[ ]||                                          ______________________/
