&+LThe blade curves like the &+Wfang &+Lof a predatory animal, blacked to a
&+Cmirror&+c sheen&+L. Along its edge, faint &+rc&+Rr&+ri&+Rm&+rs&+Ro&+rn &+Rv&+re&+Ri&+rn&+Rs&+L pulse with a dim,
&+Lhungry &n&+mglow&+L when near living &+rblood&+L. The hilt is bound in worn, black
&+Lleather and the guard is shaped like unfurled raven wings, tipped
&+Lwith &+Csilver&+L. A small &+Rr&+ru&+Rb&+ry&+L gleams at the center of the pommel,
&+Lshimmering with an inner light. When unsheathed, the dagger emits a
&+Lfaint &Nwhispering&+L sound..

According to legend, Strahd von Zarovich commissioned the dagger
during his mortal years as a weapon of ceremony. When he became the
vampire lord of Barovia, he reforged it through necromantic rites
and the Dark Powers that rule Ravenloft. The weapon became a symbol
of intimate death - used in dark rituals and executions. It is said
that the dagger drank as much blood as Strahd himself. Some say that
the blade remembers each of its victims - and that those who hold it
hear the faint echoes of their dying pleas.
