mystical scroll favor archmage~
                                             ___________________________
   _______________________-------------------                           `\
 /:--__                                                                  |
||< > |                                   _______________________________/
| \__/_________________-------------------                             |
|                                                                      |
|   To the One Whose Mind Commands the Unseen,                         |
 |                                                                      |
 | From the shadowed halls of Castle Ravenloft, I, Rahadin, Chamberlain |
 | and eternal servant to His Excellency, Count Strahd von Zarovich,    |
  | extend to you a summons most rare.                                 |
  |                                                                    |
  | The mists whisper your name - a name spoken with both reverence    |
  | and unease - and so it has reached my master's ear. He has watched |
  | your will, as you have shaped light and shadow as one might shape  |
  | molten gold. The Count has deemed you worthy of a mantle long      |
  | vacant: that of Archmage of Castle Ravenloft, a title held by none |
  | since the fall of Exethanter himself.                              |
 |                                                                    |
 | Within these walls, the air hums with ancient power. The very      |
 | stones remember spells whispered centuries ago. Here, your talents |
 | would not be confined to petty courts or trembling apprentices.    |
 | You would command the Sanctum Arcanum, a sanctified wing sealed by |
 | wards of Strahd's own design. Its libraries hold volumes thought   |
 | lost to time, tomes that breathe when opened and bleed when read.  |
 | The laboratories await your hand; the night itself, your inquiry.  |
  |                                                                    |
  | Your charge, should you accept, is simple yet eternal: to serve    |
  | the Count in all matters of the arcane. To study the forces that   |
  | bind this land and to seek understanding where others would flee.  |
  | You will find your freedom vast - within the limits of His will.   |
  | In return, the Count offers knowledge beyond mortal measure:       |
 | the secrets of life, death, and the still-beating heart of eternity. |
  |                                                                     |
  | Take heed - refusal is not punished, but it is remembered.          |
  | Acceptance, however, grants you purpose beyond mortality. When you  |
  | have resolved your affairs, present yourself to me before the moon  |
  | reaches its zenith. Speak to me of the treasures of Ravenloft, and  |
  | I shall issue your final trials. Return five treasures with this    |
  | scroll to me, and the mists will open the way.                      |
  | The Count awaits your arrival. I await your obedience.             |
  |                                                                   |
 |         &+L,_  &+g`{&+r@&+g)'                       &+b/R /4 /-/ /4 /> / /\/&n     |
 |        &+L<)')-&+g//`                       &+BHigh Chamberlain Rahadin&n     |
